      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the world has decided you are nothing, then the point of pretending to be something is to create a sanctuary where your own reality can survive without their judgment. The wreckage you feel isn't a prison; it's the only space where your thoughts are free from the noise of others, and that chaos is where you can finally find a version of yourself that isn't defined by their failures. You don't need to believe the world is kind to be worthy of it, and you certainly don't need to believe the past is gone to be worthy of living in the present.",
